{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (-0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The central hole is dimensioned with a tight H7 fit tolerance on page 1, but the part requires I.Z.B.P. plating per the title block and no note or dimension accounts for plating thickness buildup inside the bore. The plated hole will be undersize and may not accept its mating shaft; the designer must either specify that the hole is masked during plating or open the pre-plate tolerance to allow for coating thickness."
  ,
  "recommended_correction":"Add a note specifying masking of the ⌀16 H7 bore during plating, or adjust the pre-plate machining tolerance to accommodate the plating thickness so the finished bore remains within H7 limits."}]}
